<!--
    AArch64 compiler traps (`option brktrap on|off`, default on).

    Issue: AArch64 SLEIGH lowers `brk #imm16` to
    `pc = SoftwareBreakpoint(imm16, inst_next); goto [pc];`. Jump-table recovery
    cannot resolve that jump, so flow truncated it to a call followed by a
    return, and a function whose overflow or bounds check ends in a compiler
    trap printed as void and passed the value it returns to the trap.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 flow classification. `p2_lift/kuna_brktrap.rs` matches
    a BRANCHIND through the result of a `SoftwareBreakpoint` CALLOTHER in the
    same instruction whose immediate a compiler emits for a trap (#1 llvm.trap,
    #1000 GCC __builtin_trap, #0x5500-#0x55ff llvm.ubsantrap), and `flow.rs`
    replaces the jump with a no-return halt.

    P0 assertion: `option brktrap on|off`.

    Bytes assembled with `clang -c -arch arm64` (each function 16-byte aligned):
      0x100000 add_trap      adds x0,x0,x1; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #1
                             (clang -O2: if (__builtin_add_overflow(a,b,&r))
                             __builtin_trap(); return r;)
      0x100010 mul_add_trap  mul x8,x0,x1; smulh x9,x0,x1; cmp x9,x8,asr #63;
                             b.ne 1f; adds x0,x8,x0; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #1
                             (two checks sharing one trap)
      0x100030 index_gcc     cmp x0,#0xf; b.hi 1f; ldr x0,[x1,x0,lsl #3]; ret;
                             1: brk #1000 (GCC's __builtin_trap)
      0x100050 add_ubsan     adds x0,x0,x1; b.vs 1f; ret; 1: brk #0x5500
                             (clang -fsanitize-trap=signed-integer-overflow)
      0x100060 debug_trap    brk #0xf000; add x0,x0,#1; ret
                             (__builtin_debugtrap, which execution continues past)
      0x100070 debugger_bp   brk #0; add x0,x0,#1; ret

    Pass 1 (the shipped default) is the FIX: the three checked-arithmetic
    functions return their value and every compiler trap is a statement that
    ends the flow. The two debug traps keep the jump-as-call.
    Pass 2 (`option brktrap off`) reproduces the BUG: the same three print
    void and pass the value to the trap, and index_gcc returns a value
    fabricated from a call through the trap.

    The default pass runs FIRST because the console's comment database is
    keyed by function and persists across `decompile` calls: the jump-as-call
    warnings the off pass buffers would otherwise be printed in a later pass
    that does not produce them.
-->
